<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Titti</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Celtiberian people of the Jalón valley, allies of the Belli in the war with Rome that began at Segeda in 153 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Titti were one of the Celtiberian peoples of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> tributaries, probably around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalon">Jalón</a> valley in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> province. They are known almost only from Appian's account of the Celtiberian wars, which links them closely with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belli">Belli</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their institutions beyond their dependence on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belli">Belli</a>. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segeda">Segeda</a> enlarged its walls, it forced the Titti to settle there, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> treated as a breach of the treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius-sempronius-gracchus-consul-177-bc">Gracchus</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They fought with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belli">Belli</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arevaci">Arevaci</a> in the wars of 153 to 133 BCE and are last mentioned in that conflict. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a> in 133 BCE their territory was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:5.31%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Celtiberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tithii</dd></dl></aside></div>

